<title>POLAND: Polish broad money rises 1.0 pct March 1-10 - NBP.</title>
<headline>Polish broad money rises 1.0 pct March 1-10 - NBP.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland's broad money rose by 1.36 billion zlotys, or 1.0 percent, in the period March 1-10 to 139.7 billion after a 1.6 percent rise in February, preliminary central bank figures showed.</p>
<p>  BROAD POLISH MONEY		  MARCH 1-10  FEBRUARY MARCH 96</p>
<p>  month/month change (pct)		1.0	  1.6	  2.4</p>
<p>  Money in bln zlotys		   139.70     138.34    110.64</p>
<p>  Foreign currency (in bln PLN)	24.59	24.57     21.13</p>
<p>  National currency		     115.12     113.77     89.51</p>
<p>  Cash in circulation		    24.24	23.45     20.64</p>
<p>   Lending to non-financial sector   86.14	85.29     59.56</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
